// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 16 (Impl-U, Cohort Delta): the BOUNDARY
// RULE — one tape, one ledger: the P2↔wave boundary rule (E0812's
// bracket, NI(ii) "ports don't escape") extended to P5 (W2C §4's
// E4). A tape op cannot cross a wave body: the wave stages its own
// effects (contrib → J(W)) and the tape's chronicle must stay one
// linear ledger of the fallback state — records program-order-
// outside the wave only. The full tape surface is refused in-wave
// (records AND reads: under the future parallel form a tape read is
// schedule-dependent, and slice 1 refuses the whole seam rather
// than hair-split it).
ptr seam = lcell_new(1)

fn main() {
    tape<int> t = tape_new("w")
    wave {
        tape_record(t, 0, 1)
        tape_replay(t, seam)
        contrib(seam, 4, 0)
    }
}
